// What a road costs to lay on each terrain, and nothing else. Which terrains
// exist, and which of them a building may stand on or a road may be laid on,
// are facts about the game and live in the Terrain enum in sim-core; the one
// thing about a terrain that is a number lives here, because every number does
// (D6). Every variant must be listed exactly once.
//
// Water carries a cost of 0 and nothing ever reads it: no road can be laid on
// water at all. The row is here because the table describes every terrain, and
// the loader refuses a non-zero cost on ground no road can reach, so a number
// nobody reads cannot look like a knob.
(
    terrains: [
        (terrain: Plain, road_cost: 2),
        (terrain: Water, road_cost: 0),
        (terrain: Rock,  road_cost: 6),
    ],
)
